      "description": "University Jobs at EOU | Advanced Clinical Educator (Assistant Professor) – Online MSW Program Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help EOU Home HR Home HR Contacts About Union County Advanced Clinical Educator (Assistant Professor) – Online MSW Program Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application Requirements: Please submit the following: Cover letter addressing interest in EOU, professional goals, qualifications and alignment with the MSW program mission; Curriculum vitae; One-page statement of teaching philosophy; Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required for finalists); Names and contact information for three professional references. Candidates are encouraged to review the Values and Principles of Eastern Oregon University . Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. Eastern Oregon University – Oregon’s Rural University! – is a respected public, higher education institution of academic excellence. Outstanding faculty and staff thrive and together fulfill their career ambitions to serve students from all walks of life. EOU is a beautiful, quaint campus nestled in a remarkably scenic, high elevation valley populated by wonderful, community-minded citizens that have balanced work-life flexibility. Take a Virtual Tour of Eastern Oregon University . EOU offers a very attractive package of state public employee benefits including: Paid holidays Paid sick time off (8 hours/month) Individual and Family Healthcare Insurance (95%+ employer-paid medical, dental, vision) Generous Oregon Public Employee Retirement System benefits Employer-paid life insurance Discounted tuition benefits for employees and eligible dependents For more details, see EOU Prospective Employees Eastern Oregon University is an EEO Employer and welcomes applications from women, members of historically underrepresented minority groups, US Veterans, and persons with disabilities. EOU is committed to providing equal opportunity in its recruitment, admissions, educational programs, activities, and employment without illegal discrimination on the basis of age, color, disability, national origin, race, marital status, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any status as protected by state or federal law. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Advanced Clinical Educator (Assistant Professor) – Online MSW Program Classification Title Faculty Full or Part Time Full Time FTE 1.0 FTE Position Type Regular Posting Number 20110223FAC Position Summary Information- Displays to Applicant Job Description Summary Position Information: Eastern Oregon University invites applications for a full-time, 9-month Advanced Clinical Educator (Assistant Professor) to join the online Master of Social Work ( MSW ) Program. This remote faculty position will support a fully online, asynchronous graduate program with a focus on advanced generalist practice serving rural and underserved populations. Responsibilities include teaching, advising, scholarship, service, and contributions to accreditation efforts. The MSW program launched in Fall 2025; this role begins Fall 2027 and includes 45 total quarter credit hours of teaching and service over the 9-month appointment. Job Description Summary The MSW program at EOU is designed to serve adult learners, particularly those in rural and underserved communities, through a fully online, asynchronous delivery model. Operating on an 11-week quarter system, the curriculum emphasizes ethical, inclusive, and evidence-informed advanced generalist practice. The program does not require a campus residency. EOU seeks professionals who demonstrate commitment and teaching effectiveness in order to assist our students in preparing and attaining their professional goals The anticipated start date for this faculty position is September 16, 2027, with instruction beginning September, 27 2027. The appointment covers Fall, Winter, and Spring quarters, with Summer term off. Compensation is based on the successful applicant’s education and relevant teaching and social work experience. This position comes with a generous healthcare package for both employee and all family dependents, paid holidays, paid sick time, state employee retirement pension, and other fringe benefits. See Master of Social Work webpage for program information Responsibilities Teach graduate-level courses in the generalist and advanced generalist social work curriculum via asynchronous online delivery; Provide timely, substantive feedback and maintain regular communication with students; Assess student learning through varied and appropriate evaluation strategies. Advise and mentor MSW students, including support in academic and professional development; Maintain compliance with CSWE accreditation standards and contribute to accreditation documentation and preparation; Supporting program accreditation efforts ( CSWE ); Maintain an active scholarly agenda relevant to the social work profession; Collaborate with faculty and staff to support continuous program improvement; Demonstrate effective time management, attention to detail, and commitment to meeting academic deadlines. Minimum Qualifications Master of Social Work ( MSW ) from a Council on Social Work Education ( CSWE ) accredited program; Two (2) years of full-time post- MSW professional social work practice experience; Two (2) years of experience teaching core courses required of a CSWE accredited program; Evidence of competent teaching ability online. Must satisfactorily complete EOU criminal and credential background check. Having a criminal history is not an automatic bar to employment. In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Eastern Oregon University will not sponsor applicants for employment visas. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral Degree in social work or closely related field; Licensure as LCSW , LMSW , or equivalent in the applicant’s state of residence; Experience teaching graduate asynchronous online social work courses; Experience supervising master’s level social work students; Proficiency with Canvas LMS and online course development; Familiarity with CSWE accreditation and EPAS standards; Demonstrated commitment to serving diverse student populations, including adult learners. Special Instructions to Applicants Application Requirements: Please submit the following: Cover letter addressing interest in EOU , professional goals, qualifications and alignment with the MSW program mission; Curriculum vitae; One-page statement of teaching philosophy; Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required for finalists); Names and contact information for three professional references. Candidates are encouraged to review the Values and Principles of Eastern Oregon University . Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. Eastern Oregon University – Oregon’s Rural University! – is a respected public, higher education institution of academic excellence. Outstanding faculty and staff thrive and together fulfill their career ambitions to serve students from all walks of life. EOU is a beautiful, quaint campus nestled in a remarkably scenic, high elevation valley populated by wonderful, community-minded citizens that have balanced work-life flexibility. Take a Virtual Tour of Eastern Oregon University . EOU offers a very attractive package of state public employee benefits including: Paid holidays Paid sick time off (8 hours/month) Individual and Family Healthcare Insurance (95%+ employer-paid medical, dental, vision) Generous Oregon Public Employee Retirement System benefits Employer-paid life insurance Discounted tuition benefits for employees and eligible dependents For more details, see EOU Prospective Employees Eastern Oregon University is an EEO Employer and welcomes applications from women, members of historically underrepresented minority groups, US Veterans, and persons with disabilities. EOU is committed to providing equal opportunity in its recruitment, admissions, educational programs, activities, and employment without illegal discrimination on the basis of age, color, disability, national origin, race, marital status, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any status as protected by state or federal law. Salary Assistant Professor salary range is $63,328 to $79,614 per academic year. Initial assistant professor rank salary is determined by weighted years of teaching based upon the faculty union contract. Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/09/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes First Day of Application Review 11/09/2026 Quick Link to Posting https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/3629 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? EOU Website Posting Chronicle of Higher Education State Employment Service DiverseJobs.net Referral by EOU Employee HigherEdJobs.com Newspaper Other If you answered \"Newspaper\" or \"Other\" above, please give specifics here: (Open Ended Question) EOU has requirements that all employees show proof of vaccination or request and receive an approved vaccination exemption. Are you you willing to comply with this requirement? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcripts Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Veteran Preference Document To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
