      "title": "Undergrad and Graduate level Environmental Education Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "University Jobs at EOU | Undergrad and Graduate level Environmental Education Adjunct Instructor Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help EOU Home HR Home HR Contacts About Union County Undergrad and Graduate level Environmental Education Adjunct Instructor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates are encouraged to review the values and principles of Eastern Oregon University . Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. Eastern Oregon University – Oregon’s Rural University! – is a respected public, higher education institution of academic excellence. Brilliant faculty and staff thrive and together fulfill their career ambitions to serve students from all walks of life. EOU is a beautiful, quaint campus nestled in a remarkably scenic, high elevation valley populated by wonderful, community-minded citizens that have balanced work-life flexibility. Take a virtual tour of Eastern Oregon University . Minimum Requirements. Must satisfactorily complete EOU criminal and credential background check. Having a criminal history is not an automatic bar to employment. In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Eastern Oregon University will not sponsor applicants for employment visas. Special Instructions Eastern Oregon University is an EEO Employer and welcomes applications from women, members of historically underrepresented minority groups, US Veterans, and persons with disabilities. EOU is committed to providing equal opportunity in its recruitment, admissions, educational programs, activities and employment without illegal discrimination on the basis of age, color, disability, national origin, race, marital status, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any status as protected by state or federal law. Posting Details Position Information Position Number Position Title Undergrad and Graduate level Environmental Education Adjunct Instructor Job Description Summary Position Information: The Environmental Education Certificate at Eastern Oregon University is designed to equip formal and nonformal educators, natural resources professionals, and community leaders with the knowledge and skills to provide engaging and meaningful outdoor learning experiences with youth. The program is applicable for educators coming from a variety of contexts including, but not limited to, K-12 classrooms, outdoor schools, school gardens and farms, after school programs, and outdoor field days. The certificate emphasizes developing effective and inclusive outdoor teaching practices at both the instructional and programmatic level for diverse audiences. An adjunct position for one of these courses will be responsible for meeting the course and certificate outcomes with their instruction. The College of Education at Eastern Oregon University is currently seeking applicants for a part-time, adjunct to teach in undergraduate and graduate teacher licensure and certificates programs. Candidates must demonstrate a strong commitment to quality teaching, and be effective in integrating technology into instruction. Candidates should possess the ability to work collaboratively and productively with students, staff, faculty, and administration, fostering a positive and inclusive educational environment. Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills are essential, enabling the candidate to engage meaningfully with a diverse community. The candidate brings relevant life experience, education, and/or training in supporting students with a wide range of needs, ensuring that all learners are valued and supported. Additionally, they have demonstrated experience, education, or training in Environmental Education, enriching the curriculum with knowledge and practices that promote environmental awareness. Experience in designing and delivering educational or training sessions is required, including expertise in planning, curriculum development, and assessment. This background ensures the candidate can create effective, engaging, and measurable learning experiences for all students. Responsibilities Teaching responsibilities will vary depending on the specific course the adjunct instructor is qualified to teach. For the EVED courses within the Environmental Education certificate, collaboration amongst other adjuncts for continuity and scaffolding is required. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in Education, Natural Resources, Science, or related field. Three years’ experience in educational systems (formal and/or nonformal). Demonstrated life experience, education, and/or training in environmental educational Demonstrate a strong commitment to quality teaching, and be effective in integrating technology into instruction. Valid work authorization documents are required Satisfactorily complete a background check Preferred Qualifications Teaching and or learning through an online learning management system College teaching experience in K-12 Teacher Education Preparation Program Experience with an outdoor educational program Demonstrated life experience, education, and/or training in promoting and enhancing diversity, equity, and inclusion through work with historically marginalized populations. Posting Detail Information Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Summary Candidates are encouraged to review the values and principles of Eastern Oregon University . Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. Eastern Oregon University – Oregon’s Rural University! – is a respected public, higher education institution of academic excellence. Brilliant faculty and staff thrive and together fulfill their career ambitions to serve students from all walks of life. EOU is a beautiful, quaint campus nestled in a remarkably scenic, high elevation valley populated by wonderful, community-minded citizens that have balanced work-life flexibility. Take a virtual tour of Eastern Oregon University . Minimum Requirements. Must satisfactorily complete EOU criminal and credential background check. Having a criminal history is not an automatic bar to employment. In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Eastern Oregon University will not sponsor applicants for employment visas. Special Instructions Eastern Oregon University is an EEO Employer and welcomes applications from women, members of historically underrepresented minority groups, US Veterans, and persons with disabilities. EOU is committed to providing equal opportunity in its recruitment, admissions, educational programs, activities and employment without illegal discrimination on the basis of age, color, disability, national origin, race, marital status, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any status as protected by state or federal law. Quick Link to Posting https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/3287 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? EOU Website Posting Chronicle of Higher Education State Employment Service DiverseJobs.net Referral by EOU Employee HigherEdJobs.com Newspaper Other If you answered \"Newspaper\" or \"Other\" above, please give specifics here: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Veteran Preference Document Transcripts Statement of Teaching Philosophy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
