 as protected by state or federal law.** Posting Details Position Information Position Number Position Title Student Teaching Education Supervisor Job Description Summary Eastern Oregon University is currently seeking applicants for part-time, adjunct education supervisor positions in the Teacher Preparation for the Undergraduate and Master of Teaching programs within the Washington, Oregon, and Idaho areas. The Student Teacher Supervisor is responsible for instructing, coaching and supervising student teachers during their practical clinical work in school settings Oregon. Supervisors provide written and electronic evaluations of the student teacher’s performance in accordance with EOU College of Education Supervisor Handbook. In addition, the University Supervisor regularly counsels student teachers, visits them in their clinical experience site, observes and evaluates their performance and provides feedback, confers with the clinical faculty and cooperating teacher(s), and serves as a liaison between the University and the area schools. The University Supervisor must participate in the Clinical training program during the first year of employment. This recruitment is to establish an applicant pool for future part-time Adjunct Ed Supervision. The college hires part-time supervisor on a quarter by quarter basis, dependent on enrollment. If you are selected for a potential future vacancy, a college representative will contact you. Responsibilities · Observe (Virtually and in some cases Face-to- Face), mentor, and assist pre-service teachers during their student teaching. · Complete necessary observation documents electronically. Required Qualifications · Education degree from an accredited college or university. · At least 3 years of successful classroom teaching experience. · Knowledge of and experience in K-12 education. · Valid work authorization documents are required. Satisfactorily complete a background check. Preferred Qualifications · Master’s degree from an accredited college or university. · Knowledge of or experience with the co-teaching model. - Ability to observe for ‘best practices’ in K-12 classrooms. Posting Detail Information Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Summary Candidates are encouraged to review the values and principles of Eastern Oregon University . Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. Eastern Oregon University – Oregon’s Rural University! – is a respected public, higher education institution of academic excellence. Brilliant faculty and staff thrive and together fulfill their career ambitions to serve students from all walks of life. EOU is a beautiful, quaint campus nestled in a remarkably scenic, high elevation valley populated by wonderful, community-minded citizens that have balanced work-life flexibility. Take a virtual tour of Eastern Oregon University . Eastern Oregon University is an EEO Employer and welcomes applications from women, members of historically underrepresented minority groups, US Veterans, and persons with disabilities. EOU is committed to providing equal opportunity in its recruitment, admissions, educational programs, activities and employment without illegal discrimination on the basis of age, color, disability, national origin, race, marital status, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any status as protected by state or federal law. Quick Link to Posting https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/2545 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? EOU Website Posting Chronicle of Higher Education State Employment Service DiverseJobs.net Referral by EOU Employee HigherEdJobs.com Newspaper Other If you answered \"Newspaper\" or \"Other\" above, please give specifics here: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Veteran Preference Docu