l be reviewed as they are received, starting October 3, 2025. Posting Details Position Information Position Number Position Title Adjunct Instructor - Health & Human Performance Job Description Summary The College of Science, Technology, Mathematics and Health Sciences at Eastern Oregon University is recruiting for an online adjunct instructor pool to teach courses in the area of Health & Human Performance . Appointment begins based on departmental need. See webpage for full program information: https://www.eou.edu/hhp/ Responsibilities Teaching responsibilities would include online classes in the fields of health education, physical exercise, exercise science, nutrition, and kinesiology. Required Qualifications Master’s Degree in exercise science, community health, physical education or a related field from an accredited institution at the time the appointment begins. Commitment to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level is required. Documented evidence of online teaching experience in higher education Must satisfactorily complete EOU criminal and credential background check. Having a criminal history is not an automatic bar to employment. In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Eastern Oregon University does not sponsor applicants for employment visas. Preferred Qualifications PhD in exercise science, community health, physical education or a related field; candidates nearing completion of their doctorate ( ABD ) may be considered. Online teaching certification Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/03/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Summary Applicants are required to provide: 1) Letter of application (which should include why this position is attractive to the applicant, how it meets the applicant’s professional goals, and what attracts the applicant to EOU’s online program); 2) Curriculum vitae with the names, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references; 3) Transcripts (official required for finalists); 4) One-page statement of teaching philosophy. 5) Sample syllabus (use “Portfolio 1” in the online application system to upload the syllabus) 6) Sample of Learning Management System use for online courses (use “Portfolio 2” in the online application system to upload this documentation). Candidates are encouraged to review the values and principles of Eastern Oregon University . Compensation for online adjunct instructors varies by student credit hours and/or student enrollment: * Undergraduate classes enrolling 15 students or less: $47.50 per student credit hour * Undergraduate classes enrolling 16 students or more: $760.00 per credit hour Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, starting October 3, 2025. Quick Link to Posting https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/1623 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? EOU Website Posting Chronicle of Higher Education State Employment Service DiverseJobs.net Referral by EOU Employee HigherEdJobs.com Newspaper Other If you answered \"Newspaper\" or \"Other\" above, please give specifics here: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcripts Portfolio (document1) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Veteran Preference Document Portfolio (document2) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
